here; ported files say so in their header comments or commit messages.

Caelestia shell (GNU GPL-3.0)
  https://github.com/caelestia-dots/shell
  The colour service and Material scheme handling, the frame and drawer
  approach, popout behaviour, and the BlobRect goo spring (via Ryoku).

Ryoku (GNU GPL-3.0)
  https://github.com/ryoku-dev/ryoku
  The design discipline (tokens, hairlines, Latin + CJK glosses, tracked mono
  labels), motion tokens, the BlobRect goo spring, and the frosted-paper
  recipe. Ryoku itself adapts portions of:
    - Caelestia shell (GPL-3.0), as above
    - DankMaterialShell, Copyright (c) 2025 Avenge Media LLC (MIT License)
      https://github.com/AvengeMedia/DankMaterialShell
    - OkShell by John Oberhauser
  Anything taken from those parts keeps their notices.

Cave Abode (dhrruvsharma/shell, GNU GPL-3.0)
  The xianxia lock screen and its theme.

